Subject: [PATCH] Correct FEMMI observations, adjoints and posterior consistency

Base: 9762fd457d40fae88129805a0917b72c40b6cb16

Correct the P3 projected transpose and JAX Dirichlet RHS/Hessian action;
use consistent masks and relative-precision weights through MAP, Morozov,
B-mode diagnostics, catalogue reconstruction and posterior sampling.
Repair weighted RTO perturbations and report failed posterior solves.
Use the supplied energy prior in HMC; reject score-only L-BFGS objectives
while retaining explicitly approximate score sampling.

Define order-independent HCT vertex recovery and integrate HCT mass,
stiffness and loads over its polynomial subtriangles. Align C1 prior
conventions and fix constant-field coefficients in its sparsity weights.
Make legacy diagnostic failures visible to pytest. Check both SVD equations
and correct unsupported support-recovery, compactness, far-field and gauge
claims. Preserve historical benchmark values as explicitly stale pending
recalibration, rather than inventing replacement measurements.

Validation (CPU, OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1):
- Untouched base: FEMMI_REQUIRE_OPTIONAL=1 python -m pytest -q
  239 passed, 2 warnings, 538.34 s.
- Corrected full suite: FEMMI_REQUIRE_OPTIONAL=1 python -m pytest -q FEMMI/tests
  262 passed, 2 warnings in 531.86s (0:08:51).
- Eight additional sampler checks added after full-suite collection: all pass.
- Final C1 assembly/HCT checks: 9 pass.
- compileall and git diff --check pass.
- No numerical quality thresholds relaxed to accommodate changed results.

Environment: Python 3.12; NumPy 2.3.5; SciPy 1.17.0; JAX/JAXlib 0.11.2;
pytest 9.1.1; Flax 0.12.10; Optax 0.2.8; GalSim 2.8.5; Astropy 8.0.1.
All required optional dependencies were present; no optional skips allowed.

Compatibility: score-only neural priors now require sampling; energy-based
MAP must receive a consistent scalar penalty and gradient. Score samplers
remain experimental and mark a zero initial field instead of claiming it is
a posterior MAP. Non-binary weighted uncertainty and HCT results change.
The estimator remains linear-shear with a specified exterior model; this
patch does not establish continuum uniqueness or real-data validity.

Step 2 (Numba acceleration), recalibration and publication benchmarks are
intentionally separate. No unpublished draft text or results are included.

